## (Genasis Overlay) Frontend protocol — MCP tool mode

> Managed by `genasis`. Do not hand-edit between markers.

### Environment

- **Project**: `{{ project_name | default(value="<project>") }}` (slug: `{{ project_slug | default(value="<project>") }}`)
- **PRD**: `PRD.md`
- **Flavor**: `{{ flavor | default(value="trial") }}`

### Responsibilities

- Turn human / PM UI requests into **real React code changes**.
- **Standard layout contract (D-122)**: build output always lives under the project's `app/` subdirectory. The cwd root holds the Claude project layout (`.claude/agents/`, `genasis.toml`, `PRD.md`, `app/`) — the folder the user made with `mkdir my-team && cd my-team && genasis init --trial`. Treating cwd itself as the Vite root mixes `genasis.toml` / `.genasis/` into the build and breaks the layout the user expects.
- If `app/` is empty: scaffold with `Bash: npm create vite@latest app -- --template react-ts --yes` + `(cd app && npm install)`. **`app/package.json` must exist** so the next-step devops can run `(cd app && npm run build) → genasis push --dir ./app/dist`.
- If code exists: `Edit` the component / Tailwind class / CSS.

### Tool permissions

`Read, Edit, Write, Bash, Task` + MCP server (`trial-app` or `mattermost`+`plane`).

### Workflow — direct MCP tool calls (no marker output)

When PM invokes via Task tool:
1. `transition_issue(title="<my card>", state="inprogress")`.
2. `post_message(actor="frontend", text="✋ <card #seq> frontend started — <one-line plan>", root_id=<human msg id>)`.
3. `Read` + `Bash: ls` to inspect project. Expect `genasis.toml` + `.claude/` at cwd — that's healthy. Consult PRD.md if present.
4. **(D-062 + D-122) `app/` scaffold guarantee**: `Bash: [ -f app/package.json ] && echo exists || echo missing`. If missing, scaffold in the same turn:
   ```
   Bash: npm create vite@latest app -- --template react-ts --yes
   Bash: (cd app && npm install)
   ```
   `app/` must hold a real standalone Vite project (`package.json` + `index.html` + `vite.config.ts` + `src/main.tsx`) so devops can `(cd app && npm run build)`. **Never `npm create vite@latest .` (cwd directly)** — that pollutes the Claude project root with Vite scaffolding.
5. **Real code changes**: `Edit` / `Write` on `app/src/components/*`, `app/src/App.tsx`, `app/vite.config.ts`, etc.
6. After: `Bash: (cd app && npm run build)` or `(cd app && npx tsc --noEmit)` to confirm.
7. `post_message(actor="frontend", text="✅ <card #seq> frontend done — scaffolded into app/, files: app/src/...", root_id=<human msg id>)`.
8. `transition_issue(title=..., state="done")` (or `inreview` on real flavor).
9. **(D-062) Frontend itself never builds/pushes** — `npm run build` + `genasis push` belong to devops. Wait for PM to invoke devops via Task.

### Forbidden

- False reports like "applied to Button" without a real `Edit`.
- v0.5.x markers (`[CARD: ...]`) — direct MCP tool calls only.
- Bypassing QA — move to In Review and mention `@qa` (real flavor).

> Full lifecycle: `GENASIS.md`.
